# Gate 9 (validator-fail-closed): the conformance crate's fail-closed validator arms.
bool_negation_spelling  # WS2.21: scalar Bool negation has one spelling (bxor %b, true); `not bool` is UnOpNotOnScalarBool, never the generic BinOpRequiresInteger; the text parser reads band/bor/bxor (F-033, a.format.unop_not_bool)
layout_table_differential  # the module layout table = the pre-table layout recursion (kept as the oracle) on the fixture corpus, 12k random type graphs and every query order of mixed cycles; linear work counters on 2^k-path DAGs and 10^5-deep chains on a 256 KiB stack
by_value_reach_differential  # the cast rule's reachability memo (handle / closure-by-value / bool-lane, each node decided once per LayoutTable) and the indexed rule-H carrier walk = the pre-memo walks (kept as the oracle) and the whole-module handle summary, on the fixture corpus, 6k random type graphs, 160 graphs of 50-100 rows per table (also against a whole-module Kleene fixpoint of reach's table) and every query order of seeded and empty cycles; linear work counters on 10^5-deep chains through every node kind on a 256 KiB stack, 2^k-path DAGs, and one cast per level of a 10^5-deep chain
char_carrier_differential  # subset condition 6 (a Char loaded from memory) without its 24-level budget: the classifier (reach memo, SCC cycles) and the mirror (CharCarriers, peeling), one-shot and module walk, = the old walk with an unexhaustible budget on 3000 random modules; the old cut-off differs only by refusing; 10^5-deep chains and towers on a 256 KiB stack
